Z||000000||Mattyman||12-28-2001||04:15 PM||||I was just wondering what you could say when you tell someone you have a Fiero and they laugh, especially a mechanic?  Never really happened to me, except a friend of my brothernlaw thinks they are crap.  What would you say or if it has happened what did you say?<P>------------------<BR>You gotta stand for Something or your gonna fall for everything.||||reg||5
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||12-28-2001||04:49 PM||||Depends on what year they are familiar with.<P>Most people I encounter, have heard about the early  84 models,(fires, Citation suspension, poor performance compared to market hype, etc.)<P>Just be well studied in Fiero history, and let them know that Fiero owners have very collectible cars with lots of room for improvements and upgrades.<P>Make your Fiero the best it can be and watch their mouth slowly shut....<BR><P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">     <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||12-28-2001||05:00 PM||||Do the best not to smile, look em dead in the eye and say "Ok" and start talking to someone else cuz no amount of knowledge is gonna end stupidity. Ignorance is bliss, and alot of people are blissful  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/galen-sig-2k2.gif">    <BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT></B> - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/index.shtml" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||12-28-2001||05:17 PM||||if it's a mechanic or a parts counter person... laugh with them while telling them that they will never get your money or anyone's that you know.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/quad_sig_pic_1.jpg">        <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||REDHOTT88||12-28-2001||05:25 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>if it's a mechanic or a parts counter person... laugh with them while telling them that they will never get your money or anyone's that you know.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>And while you're still laughing, tell them that it won't be long until their<BR>Chevy Celebrity wagon will have it's own Forum!!!     <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/rotfl.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">      <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||12-28-2001||06:51 PM||||At lot of people just are not familiar with Fieros. The most common comment is "Didn't they catch fire?"<P>I reply. "Just the early production."<BR>I explain the weak connecting rod thing, and how they would occasionally air-mail themselves through the front of the block if the engine ran low on oil, thereby dumping vital fluids all over the catalytic converter. Seems to satisfy them.<BR>A moderately detailed explanation, delivered with conviction, usually makes them shut up lest they appear more ignorant. <P> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
